    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d368">

                <pb facs="0299" n="287" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg287"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111A.R.–N.C./46: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Erwin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-02-16T18:00:00-05:00">February 16, 1940—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4. Your no. 3, February 13, 3 p.m. By proclamation dated October 18, 1939,<anchor
                        n="45" xml:id="d368-f1"/> it was declared unlawful for the submarines of a
                        <pb facs="0300" n="288" xml:id="pg288"/> foreign belligerent state,
                    including both commercial submarines and submarines which are ships of war, to
                    enter ports or territorial waters of the United States, exclusive of the Canal
                    Zone, except in case of <hi rendition="#italic">force majeure</hi>. The proposal
                    of the Uruguayan delegate to the Inter-American Neutrality Committee is
                    therefore one which has already been adopted by the United States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
